.TH CLRU_DESTROY 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
clru_destroy \- destroy an LRU cache and set pointer to NULL
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <clrucache.h>

clru_destroy(name);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Calls __clrucache_destroy() to evict all remaining entries (invoking
the eviction callback for each while the mutex is held), destroy the
internal map, and free all memory. Then sets name to NULL.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
name  Cache variable to destroy (will be set to NULL after destruction)
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Safe to call when name is NULL (no-op).
Must be called only after all other threads have stopped using the cache.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR clru_construct (3),
.BR __clrucache_destroy (3),
.BR clrucache_create_full (3)
